<title>USA: NY business loans down $219 mln in Jan 8 week.</title>
<headline>NY business loans down $219 mln in Jan 8 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $219 million to $43,097 million in the week ended January 8, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $219 million to $43,334 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $15.365 billion to $794.285 billion.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
